domain CONFLICT:
  description "Determine whether current accepted sources settle an unresolved V3 norm conflict."
evidence SCHEMA:
  |
    V3 norm evaluator returns zero legal actions and character_norm_conflict when
    no applicable registered legal fallback resolves the restriction conflict.
    Backend now preserves this receipt while skipping the empty provider lane.
evidence ENGINE:
  |
    The engine retains static policy selection and forceOffense/basic_attack paths.
    The normal turn uses this engine after agent decision generation. The inspected
    binding contract does not state a response for an unresolved empty action set.
premise AUTHORITY:
  |
    ADR0030 requires legality revalidation and conflict receipts. R2/ADR0039 D1
    require fixed compiler behavior, not permission to invent a turn-consuming
    no-op or a new external failure/retry contract.
premise HISTORICAL_UNKNOWN:
  |
    At the initial check the producing runtime behavior and governing clause
    were unknown. ACCEPTED_OUTCOME below resolves this historical unknown.
decision INITIAL_CHECK based_on SCHEMA, ENGINE, AUTHORITY:
  |
    The initial check kept vt102 incomplete until conflict behavior was evidenced.
    Continue authorized local tests and immutable-binding verification.
    If sources do not settle the behavior, present the exact alternatives to the
    owner before dependent runtime changes. No deployment or remote writes.
evidence ACCEPTED_OUTCOME:
  |
    Accepted ADR0011 Action and relationship semantics defines unexpected runtime
    empty-set behavior: declared legal fallback or wait, with a conflict receipt.
    Accepted requirement v6 R3 allows awareness-gated conscious guidance only
    when applicable; ADR0030 preserves those applicable boundaries.
decision CORRECT based_on SCHEMA, ENGINE, AUTHORITY, ACCEPTED_OUTCOME:
  |
    Preserve the frozen qualified programs. Overlay guidance statements using
    current facts, applicability, exceptions and awareness. Gate every engine
    action substitution against the V4 norm result and use its legal fallback
    or specified wait for an empty set. Recompute for later temporal boundaries.
    Preserve the conflict receipt even when the provider lane is skipped.
    Verify forced offense and exact skill rejection without rewriting legacy
    battles or accepting downstream lifecycle/Stage completion.
